# DF CLONE-ATTACK rig (14z-101) — the maintainer's field question: Phobos'
# DF clones appear and move correctly, but do they properly ATTACK
# (mechanical issue vs beams not rendering)? This rig activates DF with
# poked stocks and then fires the 236+LP freeze ray TWICE inside the DF
# window (the 83b spacing — the seq-D thunk shifts frame-pinned inputs, so
# two spaced attempts guarantee one lands while DF is live), plus one
# PRE-DF control ray so the non-DF projectile shape is in the same run.
#
# Runs unchanged on native vsav2 and the merged build (replay-85 doctrine);
# tenant/leg chosen by POKES:
# POKES="1400:ff8782:10;1450:ff8782:10;1500:ff8782:10;1400:ff8b82:03;1450:ff8b82:03;1500:ff8b82:03;3100:ff8509:03;3120:ff8509:03"
# (P2 = Victor 0x03, same id both games; stocks poked so DF is not the
#  seq-0x0A downgrade.)
#
# Measure with DUMPS over both pools + obj_records_dump at the ray windows:
# native clones firing = extra beam objects per attempt vs the pre-DF
# control; ours must match at the object level (mechanical) AND draw them
# (graphical — the OBJ dump is the render-layer check).
300-305 sys=C1
420-425 sys=C2
800-803 sys=S1
940-943 sys=S2
1100-1102 p2=R
1160-1162 p2=R
1300-1302 p1=1
1360-1362 p2=1
# PRE-DF control ray (the 83b measured-good input)
2900-2902 p1=D
2903-2905 p1=DR
2906-2908 p1=R1
# activate Dark Force: HP+HK with stocks poked at f3100/f3120
3260-3263 p1=36
# DF ray #1 (well inside the ~360f window opening at ~3288)
3400-3402 p1=D
3403-3405 p1=DR
3406-3408 p1=R1
# DF ray #2
3540-3542 p1=D
3543-3545 p1=DR
3546-3548 p1=R1
5000 wait
